Z||000000||3fifty||01-23-2001||08:09 PM||||I have a 85 GT V6 as a project car. If you<BR>don't have an endless wallet, is it possible<BR>to cut the factory springs to lower front,<BR>rear instead of buying aftermarket springs?<BR>If so, how much off each spring will drop<BR>X amount of inches on the car?<P>Thanks!!!!!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000001||MrPBody||01-23-2001||08:41 PM||||You can do it.  I have, for the $ame rea$on.  Cutting the stock springs will stiffen the ride as well as lowering the car.  I don't know an infallible guide for how much to cut.  I suggest cutting a little -- maybe half-coil increments -- then see how you like it.  You can always cut more but not less.<P>Try searching previous posts for more detailed info and other points of view.<BR>||||reg||1
